Far from posturing, I've been consistently encouraging specific
changes in attitude, among the group of people here, towards the dev
team.  Instead of endorsing "they can do what they want and we just
have to shut up", I wonder how much different the situation would be,
in regards to progress on development of the game, if the dominant
attitude among the community was instead "let's apply pressure on the
dev team that we want progress, and if they don't help the commmunity
in this regard, they'll lose our respect, and their authority over the
game, as we move on with our own initiative".

But that doesn't happen.  Yes, there's grumbling.  But there's a
strong enabling streak among many of the vocal nethack players, which
says time and again that we're nothing but indebted to the dev team,
that we have no right to complain, "program your own fucking game, the
source is right there", and much weirder "arguments" like "it's really
not that bad of a game as is, so we don't need a new version" and
"it's just a game, nothing to get worked up about".  Etc.

There exists here a perverted sort of respect for the way the dev team
has operated.  The lone wolf attitude, in all its forms, KILLS
attempts at community organizing and effective action here over and
over and over.

So, short answer on specifics?  How about we all recognize that the
dev team has failed us, stop cutting them slack after 5 years, apply
pressure on them, and integrate the idea that the community needs to
be serious about creating its own project if it wants a better game.

